    "summary_one_sentence": "After a volatile 19-year-old delinquent named Tommy is abducted following a night out, he awakens chained in the basement of an eccentric Yorkshire family determined to force him into a twisted process of moral rehabilitation.",
    "summary_short": "Tommy is a reckless 19-year-old living a life fueled by drugs, party culture, and senseless violence in Yorkshire. His wild lifestyle comes to a screeching halt when he is kidnapped off the streets by a mysterious man named Chris. Waking up chained in the basement of a remote country home, Tommy discovers he is held captive by Chris and his wife Kathryn, a deeply unsettling couple. Forced to comply with their disturbing psychological mind games, Tommy must navigate their bizarre conditioning methods while desperately seeking a way to escape.",
    "summary_long": "Tommy, a 19-year-old gang leader, spends his nights causing chaos, engaging in reckless violence, and documenting his criminal acts. After a night of heavy drinking and drug use, Tommy becomes separated from his friends on the street and is suddenly abducted by a shadowy assailant. He awakens chained by his neck inside the basement of an isolated country house in Yorkshire. His captors are Chris and his wife Kathryn, a deeply strange couple living upstairs with their visibly terrified young son and an intimidated housekeeper. Chris explains that he intends to subject Tommy to a rigorous regime of discipline, rewards, and psychological conditioning to reform his unruly nature and make him a 'good boy.' At first, Tommy violently resists his captivity and desperately tries to negotiate or break free. Over time, however, as Chris uses a mix of harsh punishments and strange emotional validation, Tommy’s sense of reality and resistance begin to waver. The line between prisoner and twisted family member blurs as Tommy confronts his past behavior while surviving his captors' dark, unpredictable motives. Ultimately, Tommy is forced to navigate complex psychological mind games and decide how far he will go to regain his freedom.",
    "synopsis": "Good Boy is a dark, psychological thriller that explores themes of control, trauma, and forced redemption. The story follows Tommy, a volatile 19-year-old youth who revels in antisocial behavior, drugs, and violence with his peers. Following a chaotic night out, Tommy finds himself abducted and imprisoned in the dark cellar of an isolated Yorkshire estate. He quickly learns he has been taken hostage by Chris and Kathryn, an unconventional married couple who aim to forcibly rehabilitate him into a submissive, reformed 'good boy' through a bizarre combination of strict discipline, rewards, and mind games. Operating like a dark, absurdist fairy tale, the narrative follows Tommy as he navigates the fragile dynamics of this eerie household while attempting to outwit his captors and secure his escape.",
